<title>CHILE: Drought-hit Chile orders power-saving measures.</title>
<headline>Drought-hit Chile orders power-saving measures.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile will impose from May a series of measures to save electricity as a result of a severe drought which has cut power output from dams, the country's main source of energy, said a top official.</p>
<p>The steps include reducing the voltage of power supplies by up to five percent of the level required by law, said Alejandro Jadresic, president of the National Energy Commission, Chile's equivalent of an energy ministry.</p>
<p>The government will also order public organizations to restrict decorative lighting and reduce lighting in some public places, Jadresic said in a statement.</p>
</text>
